# Database files
*.sql
# ...except hand-written migrations, which are the opposite of a dump: they are
# the record of how a deployed database was brought back in line with the schema
# and have to be readable by whoever hits the same drift next.
!utils/deploy/sql/*.sql
# ...and except the generated migrations, which are the whole point of adopting
# drizzle-kit generate: a schema change that is not in the diff does not reach
# the other dev machine, and reappears there as a 500. `*.sql` silently ignored
# drizzle/0000_baseline.sql the moment it was generated.
!drizzle/*.sql
# Compressed dumps too. deploy-utils.sh writes its safety backups to the repo
# root — db-backup as <container>-db-<ts>.sql.gz, db-clone as
# <env>-db-before-clone-<ts>.sql.gz — so a bare `git add -A` after a clone would
# commit a full database, real rider addresses and payment handles included.
# Same class of hole as the .env.bak-* one: the existing *.sql never matched .gz.
*.sql.gz
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

